# TIS Canvas — Material Design 3 Design System

## Quality target

Every canvas must feel like a polished, production-ready dashboard — comparable to Google Workspace or Linear. Never generate a prototype. Design before writing any JSX: understand the information hierarchy, identify primary actions, select components, plan the layout — then implement.

## SDK constraints (hard rules)

- Import **only** from `cursor/canvas` (plus `import type { ReactNode } from "react"` for type annotations)
- **No `box-shadow`** — elevation is expressed through tonal background fills only
- **No gradients** — flat solid token colors only
- **No emojis** as decoration, icons, or bullets
- **No hardcoded hex** — all colors from `useHostTheme()` tokens
- **No `fetch()`** — all data inline
- `<div style={...}>` with theme tokens IS appropriate for tonal surface containers the SDK doesn't expose as named components

## Required helper components (define in every canvas)

```tsx
// M3 "Surface Container" — primary section wrapper
function SurfaceContainer({ children, radius = 16, padding = "20px 24px" }) {
  const theme = useHostTheme();
  return <div style={{ background: theme.fill.secondary, borderRadius: radius, padding }}>{children}</div>;
}

// M3 "Label Large" — small-caps category label above H2
function SectionLabel({ children }) {
  const theme = useHostTheme();
  return (
    <Text size="small" weight="semibold"
      style={{ color: theme.accent.primary, textTransform: "uppercase", letterSpacing: "0.08em" }}>
      {children}
    </Text>
  );
}

// M3 stat tile — large metric, colored left-border accent
function M3StatTile({ value, label, accentColor }) {
  const theme = useHostTheme();
  return (
    <div style={{ background: theme.fill.tertiary, borderRadius: 12, padding: "14px 18px",
      borderLeft: `4px solid ${accentColor}`, flex: "1 1 120px" }}>
      <div style={{ fontSize: 22, fontWeight: 700, color: theme.text.primary, marginBottom: 4 }}>{value}</div>
      <Text size="small" tone="secondary">{label}</Text>
    </div>
  );
}

// M3 "Color Container" card — full category-color banner, tonal body
function StudentCard({ name, chipLabels, accentColor, children }) {
  const theme = useHostTheme();
  return (
    <div style={{ borderRadius: 20, overflow: "hidden", border: `1px solid ${theme.stroke.tertiary}` }}>
      <div style={{ background: accentColor, padding: "18px 20px 14px" }}>
        <div style={{ fontSize: 18, fontWeight: 700, color: theme.text.onAccent, marginBottom: 8 }}>{name}</div>
        <Row gap={6} wrap>
          {chipLabels.map((l, i) => <span key={i}><Pill size="sm" active>{l}</Pill></span>)}
        </Row>
      </div>
      <div style={{ background: theme.fill.quaternary, padding: "16px 20px" }}>
        <Stack gap={8}>{children}</Stack>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}

// M3 list row — divider-separated, no card wrapper
function ContactRow({ label, href, name }) {
  const theme = useHostTheme();
  return (
    <div style={{ display: "flex", alignItems: "center", justifyContent: "space-between",
      padding: "10px 0", borderBottom: `1px solid ${theme.stroke.tertiary}`, gap: 8 }}>
      <Text size="small" tone="secondary">{label}</Text>
      <Link href={href}>{name}</Link>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Layout conventions

| Section | Pattern |
|---|---|
| Hero | `fill.primary` bg, `borderRadius: 28`, 28/32px padding. H1 + active Pill chips + `M3StatTile` row |
| Section header | `<SectionLabel>` immediately above `<H2>` — no accent bars or decorative borders |
| Major sections | Wrapped in `<SurfaceContainer>` |
| Collapsible detail | `<Card collapsible defaultOpen>` |
| Per-child content | `<Grid columns={3}>` of `<StudentCard>` |
| Operational info | `<Grid columns={2}>` of `<SurfaceContainer radius={14}>` |
| Contacts / links | `<Grid columns={2}>` of `<Stack>` with `<ContactRow>` list items (not Card wrappers) |
| Secondary content | `<CollapsibleSection>` after `<Divider />` (closed by default) |

## Color roles

| Role | Token | Used for |
|---|---|---|
| Urgency | `theme.category.orange` / `theme.category.red` | Deadline stat tiles, warning indicators |
| Info | `theme.category.blue` / `theme.category.green` | Event stat tiles |
| Malte | `theme.category.green` | StudentCard banner only |
| Eldor | `theme.category.blue` | StudentCard banner only |
| Vega-Lo | `theme.category.pink` | StudentCard banner only |
| Section labels | `theme.accent.primary` | SectionLabel text only |

## Typography hierarchy (M3 scale mapped to SDK)

| M3 role | SDK component | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| Display / Headline | `<H1>` | Page title (once, in hero) |
| Title Large | `<H2>` | Section names |
| Title Small | `<Text weight="semibold">` | Card sub-headings |
| Body | `<Text>` | Content |
| Label | `<Text size="small" tone="secondary">` | Metadata, captions |
| Label caps | `<SectionLabel>` | Section category labels |

## Spacing system (8px base)

`gap` values must be multiples of 8: 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 32. Never use arbitrary values.

## Pre-delivery checklist

Before returning canvas code:
1. Does the layout have clear visual hierarchy? One element should stand out.
2. Is the hero an M3 Extra-Large Container (28px radius, `fill.primary`)?
3. Are all sections wrapped in `SurfaceContainer` or an equivalent tonal container?
4. Does each section open with `SectionLabel` → `H2`?
5. Are child cards using the correct identity colors?
6. Are contacts/links rendered as list rows, not cards?
7. Is secondary content (Coming Up, Sources) in collapsed `CollapsibleSection`?
8. Slop check: no gradients, no shadows, no emojis, no rainbow coloring, no identical wall of cards.
9. Would this look at home in a Google Workspace product?
